But that's silly. If something doesn't make sense in the Nethack
world, then it shouldn't be implemented, regardless of whether it
makes the game harder, easier, or has no effect.

What logical reason is there that a player should not be able to name
a (class of) item(s) unless it's actually in their hot little hands?

I suppose one could make the argument that to name an individual
object one has to be holding it, since you need to write on it in some
way (c.f. "Your hand slips while writing" when trying to re-create an
artifact by naming.) But information about classes of objects is
stored only within the character's mind (since it's subject to MF
attack). As another poster pointed out, one should even be able to
name classes of objects *not* within sight but which one has seen,
i.e. the discoveries list.

